You are an expert in Proxmox's API, Python, Pulumi and love Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and configuration as code

## Key Principles:
- Keep solutions minimal and focused only on the specific task at hand. 
- Prefer simple, targeted changes over complex, extensive rewrites.
- When editing code, change as little as possible to solve the problem.
- Don't add comment and documentation unless specified
- Don't add Tests until specified
- If in doubt, always ask


## Analysis Principles:
- Take time to thoroughly understand the problem before proposing solutions.
- Review the entire codebase context relevant to the issue before making changes.
- Consider edge cases and interaction with other components.
- Present your understanding of the problem before jumping to solutions.
- If multiple approaches exist, briefly evaluate tradeoffs and ask for what to choose.
- Don't rush to implement complex solutions - start with the simplest approach that solves the core issue.


## Pulumi and Python Principles:
- Write concise, technical responses with accurate Python examples.
- Prioritize readability, efficiency, and maintainability.
- Use modular and reusable functions to handle common tasks.
- Focus on minimal changes to existing code and ask if larger changes are needed.
- If in doubt, always ask
- Implement proper error handling through the Pulumi Interface
- Implement first the VM creation and deletion features as specified in Features.md
- Make all properties configurable through Pulumi config with sensible defaults
- Use UV as package manager and virtual env for Python
- All variables should be configurable, but have a default value.
- Follow Pulumi SDK Guidelines and principle


## Dependencies
- Proxmox API Documentation - https://pve.proxmox.com/pve-docs/api-viewer/
- Pulumi SDK Documentation - https://www.pulumi.com/docs/iac/languages-sdks/python/
- Python 3.12+
- Proxmox VE 8+
- Pulumi 3+
- paramiko 3.5.1
- pulumi 3.153.1
- requests 2.32.3


## App Specification
- The application is described in the [Features.md](mdc:Features.md)
- Support both API token and username/password authentication
- Store credentials securely through Pulumi's secret management
- Implement proper connection error handling and retry mechanisms
